00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:25.150
These links will be more extensive and take you places you want to go.
这些链接会更全面，带你们去你们想去的地方。

487
00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.650
So I just want to put that out there.
所以我只是想说明一下。

488
00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.170
Very proud of you.
为你感到骄傲。

489
00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:28.830
Thank you.
谢谢。

490
00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:29.410
Very proud of you.
真的为你感到骄傲。

491
00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:33.810
And the other thing we're excited to share with you is that we have partnered again with
另一件我们很高兴与大家分享的事是，我们再次与

492
00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:34.570
Cartooner Radio.
Cartooner Radio 合作了。

493
00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:40.270
You know, they do amazing animation of podcasts, and they are going to do the first six episodes
你们知道，他们制作的播客动画非常棒，他们将为我们重温《办公室》第一季的

494
00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:46.690
from season one of our rewatch of The Office, and they're going to do sort of like the highlights
前六集制作动画，他们会挑选出我们讨论过的内容的

495
00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.650
of things that we talked about.
精华部分。

496
00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:49.830
And they're so fun.
它们非常有趣。

497
00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:54.270
They're up on our YouTube page, our Office Ladies YouTube page, and you can watch them.
它们已经在我们的 YouTube 页面，也就是我们的 Office Ladies YouTube 页面上了，你们可以去观看。

498
00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:56.010
And we hope you like them.
希望你们会喜欢。

499
00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:01.210
Yeah, the cool thing about it is that we were able to add our personal photos.
是的，最酷的地方在于我们能够加入自己的私人照片。

500
00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:05.010
So it's like a 10-minute highlight of each episode.
所以每一集都有大约 10 分钟的精彩集锦。

501
00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:11.870
But like, for example, in the pilot, we flash up all of our personal photos from the pilot.
比如在试播集中，我们展示了所有试播集里的个人照片。

502
00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.350
And Angela, I have to share something.
安吉拉，我得分享一件事。

503
00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:21.150
So when we were looking for what to share visually from Diversity Day, we talk a little bit about
当我们寻找在“多元日”那一集里要展示的视觉素材时，我们聊到了

504
00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:24.230
like how great the script was and how I still have my script.
剧本有多棒，以及我至今还留着我的剧本。

505
00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:26.270
And so I thought, oh, I know.
于是我想，噢，我知道了。

506
00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:31.630
I'll take a picture of my script from Diversity Day so we can flash it up in this video.
我可以拍一张我那份“多元日”剧本的照片，这样我们就能在视频里展示它了。

507
00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:32.010
Right.
没错。

508
00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.790
So I went digging for it.
于是我就去翻找它。

509
00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:38.710
And first of all, my script from Diversity Day is on blue paper.
首先，我那份“多元日”剧本是用蓝色纸印的。

510
00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:40.910
Oh, so that was the second version.
噢，那是第二个版本。

511
00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.950
Yes, I was going to explain.
是的，我正要解释。

512
00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:46.670
That's how they would distinguish the different drafts of a script.
他们就是用这种方式来区分剧本的不同草稿。

513
00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:49.290
So first, they would give it to us on white paper.
起初，他们会给我们白纸印的版本。

514
00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:54.690
And then they would either give you a whole new printout on blue paper,
然后他们要么会给你一份全新的蓝色纸打印件，

515
00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:58.550
or if there were just a few changes, they'd just give you blue pages.
要么如果只有少量改动，他们就只给你几页蓝色的纸。

516
00:20:58.850 --> 00:20:59.010
Right.
没错。

517
00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:03.630
And then it was your job to go in and take out the white page and put in the blue page
你的工作就是把原来的白纸抽出来，换上蓝色的纸，

518
00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:04.390
for the rewrite.
作为重写后的版本。

519
00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:07.170
And then the third draft would be pink pages.
第三稿就会是粉色的纸。

520
00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.970
And then I think it was like yellow, green.
然后我想应该是黄色、绿色之类的。

521
00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.370
And then I feel like it went back to white.
之后感觉又变回了白色。

522
00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:16.530
No, I think every once in a while we got to orange, but that was very rare.
不，我觉得偶尔我们也会用到橙色，但那非常少见。

523
00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:17.230
Yeah.
是啊。

524
00:21:17.390 --> 00:21:19.510
And those were usually loose pages.
而且那些通常都是散页。

525
00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:19.950
Yes.
没错。

526
00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:20.910
They weren't the whole script.
它们不是完整的剧本。

527
00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:25.970
But sometimes by the end of the week, you'd have like this multicolored script.
但有时候到了周末，你的剧本就会变得五颜六色的。

528
00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:29.090
Well, anyway, this script was all blue.
总之，这份剧本全是蓝色的。

529
00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:33.810
So I guess they did one big rewrite and they printed it out on blue.
所以我猜他们进行了一次大改，然后直接用蓝纸打印了出来。

530
00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.470
I don't have any other color pages.
我没有其他颜色的页面了。

531
00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:40.450
However, at the very end of my script, I have five white pages.
不过，在剧本的最后，我有五页白纸。

532
00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.270
You guys, I want you to know Jenna brought her script in.
各位，我想让你们知道，珍娜把她的剧本带来了。

533
00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:44.230
She's holding it.
她正拿着它。

534
00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:45.030
I'm looking at it.
我正在看呢。

535
00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.110
And what did you write on the front of it?
你在封面上写了什么？

536
00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.110
Did you write Pam?
你写的是“帕姆”吗？

537
00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:48.530
Pam.
帕姆。

538
00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:50.070
I wrote Pam.
我写了帕姆。

539
00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:52.370
So everyone knows that's your script.
这样大家就知道那是你的剧本了。

540
00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:53.350
That's so cute.
太可爱了。

541
00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:55.070
Well, that was a thing back then.
嗯，那时候大家都这样。

542
00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:58.370
Like if you didn't put your name on it, anyone might pick it up.
如果你不在上面写名字，别人可能会拿错。

543
00:21:58.770 --> 00:21:59.470
It's true.
确实。

544
00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:02.710
Well, I was like, what are the white pages at the end?
我当时就在想，最后那几页白纸是什么？

545
00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.710
Do you know what it is, lady?
你知道那是什么吗，女士？

546
00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:05.830
No.
不知道。

547
00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:06.410
What is it?
那是什么？

548
00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:08.870
It's my Pam document.
那是我的“帕姆”文档。

549
00:22:09.610 --> 00:22:10.950
I printed it out.
我把它打印了出来。

550
00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:12.530
I three-hole punched it.
我还用三孔打孔机给它打了孔。

551
00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:14.790
And I attached it to the back of my script.
我把它贴在了剧本的背面。

552
00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:19.810
And I remember I did that for season one of The Office.
我记得我在拍《办公室》第一季的时候做过这件事。

553
00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:22.090
Lady, your theater nerd heart.
天哪，你那颗热爱戏剧的心。

554
00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:22.990
I know.
我知道。

555
00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:24.530
Is so wonderful.
真是太棒了。

556
00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:30.550
And I'm so excited I found this because I couldn't find it on my computer.
我很高兴找到了这个，因为我在电脑里怎么也找不到它了。

557
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:36.790
So this is now the only copy I have is this hard copy that I printed and attached to the
所以现在我手里唯一的副本就是这份打印出来并贴在

558
00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:38.470
back of my Diversity Day script.
《多元文化日》剧本背面的纸质版。

559
00:22:38.470 --> 00:22:41.350
And I have to read you something from it.
我得给你读读上面的内容。

560
00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:43.030
I want to hear all of it.
我想听听全部内容。

561
00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:47.130
I mean, I wish I had this for all about Pam Beasley.
我是说，真希望关于帕姆·比斯利的一切我都有记录。

562
00:22:48.910 --> 00:22:50.470
But here we go.
好了，我们开始吧。

563
00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:55.530
I have this section where I'm really trying to figure out Pam and Roy's relationship.
我这部分内容是在努力理清帕姆和罗伊的关系。

564
00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:58.070
And so I wrote this prompt.
所以我写下了这个提示。

565
00:22:58.090 --> 00:22:59.670
What was your biggest fight?
你们吵过最大的架是什么？

566
00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:05.050
I wrote, our biggest fight ever was the time that I told him that if I found out that he
我写道，我们吵得最凶的一次，是我告诉他，如果我发现他

567
00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:10.410
committed a murder that I would turn him into the police, like if they didn't know who did
犯了谋杀罪，我会去报警，比如如果警方不知道凶手是谁，

568
00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:12.810
it and he wasn't planning to turn himself in.
而他又不打算自首的话。

569
00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:17.270
He got really, really mad and said that families are supposed to protect each other.
他当时非常非常生气，说家人之间应该互相保护。

570
00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:20.110
And I said, yeah, but not from murder.
我说，是啊，但谋杀可不行。

571
00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:25.310
He said, what if he was really, really sorry and I could tell that he would never murder
他说，如果他真的真的非常后悔，而且我能看出他再也不会

572
00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:26.010
someone again?
杀人了呢？

573
00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:27.530
I don't know.
我不知道。

574
00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:29.710
I still think I'd probably turn him in.
但我还是觉得我可能会去举报他。

575
00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:30.970
That's amazing.
太绝了。

576
00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:31.850
Yeah.
是啊。

577
00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:32.830
That's amazing.
太绝了。

578
00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:38.030
And that it's such like one of those hypothetical bullshit things that you get in a fight about
这就像那种当你现实中相处不顺时，会拿来吵架的胡扯假设性问题。

579
00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:40.770
because the real things aren't working.
因为现实中的问题解决不了。

580
00:23:41.030 --> 00:23:41.390
Yeah.
没错。

581
00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:45.890
So you don't talk about the real things and then you have all of this pent up stuff about
所以你们不去谈论现实问题，反而把所有的积怨都发泄在

582
00:23:45.890 --> 00:23:46.530
a hypothetical.
一个假设性问题上。

583
00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:54.190
Well, I think it kind of touched on a type of disconnect in their like fundamental values,
嗯，我觉得这触及了他们价值观根本上的某种脱节，

584
00:23:54.790 --> 00:23:55.530
you know?
你知道吗？

585
00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:55.990
Yeah.
是的。

586
00:23:55.990 --> 00:24:03.850
Like Roy values family loyalty over everything and Pam sort of is a rule follower and feels
比如罗伊把家庭忠诚看得高于一切，而帕姆算是个循规蹈矩的人，觉得

587
00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:10.550
like she has a sort of moral obligation to the world that sometimes could supersede the
自己对世界有一种道德义务，这种义务有时会凌驾于

588
00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:10.910
family.
家庭之上。

589
00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:11.390
Yes.
没错。

590
00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:11.710
Yeah.
是啊。

591
00:24:11.910 --> 00:24:13.530
I was like, that's really interesting.
我当时就觉得，这真的很有意思。

592
00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:20.010
I also wrote, I used to be an illustrator, but Roy told me it was time for us to get regular
我还写道，我曾经是个插画师，但罗伊告诉我，我们该找份正经

593
00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:20.530
jobs.
工作了。

594
00:24:20.530 --> 00:24:25.510
I used to just be a receptionist on the side while I drew and tried to get work as an illustrator.
我以前只是兼职做前台，同时画画并尝试寻找插画工作。

595
00:24:26.090 --> 00:24:30.430
I'm artistic, but I've given it up to have a more stable life and job.
我很有艺术天赋，但我为了过上更稳定的生活和工作放弃了它。

596
00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:31.890
That is great.
那太棒了。

597
00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.650
Because for me, that fills in that question of like, why is Pam there?
因为对我来说，这填补了那个问题，比如帕姆为什么会在那里？

598
00:24:37.890 --> 00:24:39.350
Why is she the receptionist?
她为什么会做前台？

599
00:24:39.470 --> 00:24:44.230
Why does she seem so beat down in this job on top of everything else?
为什么除了其他一切之外，她在工作中看起来如此受挫？

600
00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:49.870
It seems like a real step back for her just being there.
待在那里对她来说似乎真的是一种倒退。

601
00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:50.730
Yeah.
没错。

602
00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:57.250
I felt like I needed to answer those questions for myself when I started the job.
我刚开始这份工作时，就觉得我需要亲自回答这些问题。

603
00:24:57.950 --> 00:25:01.250
Theater students out there, how about that?
各位戏剧专业的学生，觉得怎么样？

604
00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:05.790
Background work, building your character, things people don't ever see.
背景工作、塑造角色，这些人们永远看不到的东西。

605
00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:07.270
It's true.
确实如此。

606
00:25:07.690 --> 00:25:12.810
Well, thank you very much to Cartuna for asking us to dig around in our personal photos.
非常感谢Cartuna邀请我们去翻找自己的私人照片。

607
00:25:12.810 --> 00:25:15.590
Because now I have my Pam document back.
因为现在我找回了我的帕姆档案。

608
00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:16.030
That's right.
没错。

609
00:25:16.190 --> 00:25:20.210
And you guys, I'll share in our stories where you can find our animated highlights of the
还有各位，我会分享到我们的快拍里，你们可以在那里找到我们

610
00:25:20.210 --> 00:25:21.950
first six episodes of Office Ladies.
《办公室女士》前六集的动画集锦。

611
00:25:22.190 --> 00:25:23.930
And you can also find them at the link in bio.
你们也可以通过个人简介里的链接找到它们。

612
00:25:24.270 --> 00:25:24.950
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

613
00:25:25.070 --> 00:25:26.930
Because Jenna's updated the link in bio.
因为珍娜更新了个人简介里的链接。

614
00:25:27.150 --> 00:25:27.690
Yes, I have.
没错，我更新了。

615
00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:28.790
All right.
好的。

616
00:25:28.870 --> 00:25:30.170
Well, Angela, now I'm very excited.
那么，安吉拉，我现在非常兴奋。

617
00:25:30.310 --> 00:25:31.510
I'm going to turn it over to you.
我要把话筒交给你了。

618
00:25:31.910 --> 00:25:34.790
You watched the webisode Blackmail.
你看了网络剧《勒索》。

619
00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:35.990
Yes, I did.
是的，我看了。

620
00:25:35.990 --> 00:25:37.090
And it is so delicious.
而且它太精彩了。

621
00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:38.390
It features Creed.
主角是克里德。

622
00:25:39.030 --> 00:25:41.450
First of all, I want you guys to know where you can find these.
首先，我想让大家知道去哪里能找到这些剧集。

623
00:25:41.450 --> 00:25:45.910
All of the webisodes are on Peacock, but they're labeled a little different.
所有的网络剧都在Peacock上，但它们的标签有点不同。

624
00:25:46.190 --> 00:25:52.850
You have to go to the tile that says The Office, like the original Office, not the Superfan
你必须点击写着《办公室》的那个板块，就是原版《办公室》，不是“超级粉丝”

625
00:25:52.850 --> 00:25:53.630
versions.
版本。

626
00:25:53.950 --> 00:25:58.450
And then under that, you have to click on a little tab that says Collections.
然后在那个板块下，你得点击一个写着“合集”的小标签。

627
00:25:58.770 --> 00:26:03.350
And then under that, scroll down, and there's a little thing that says Digital Series.
接着在下面往下滑，有一个写着“数字系列”的小东西。

628
00:26:03.350 --> 00:26:08.910
I don't want to get in their business, but I guess I do.
我不想干涉他们的业务，但我想我还是得说。

629
00:26:09.310 --> 00:26:11.750
Why are you making it so hard to find these?
你们为什么要把这些弄得这么难找？

630
00:26:12.110 --> 00:26:13.630
Yeah, you do have to dig.
没错，确实得费点功夫找。

631
00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:16.150
And also, we always called them webisodes.
而且，我们一直管它们叫网络剧。

632
00:26:16.350 --> 00:26:18.670
So I guess they call them digital series.
所以我想他们管这叫数字系列。

633
00:26:18.930 --> 00:26:21.490
But that's where they live, and there's a bunch of them, and they're fantastic.
但它们就在那儿，有很多集，而且非常棒。

634
00:26:21.930 --> 00:26:24.530
And today, I want to highlight Blackmail.
今天，我想重点介绍一下《勒索》。

635
00:26:25.510 --> 00:26:31.230
It is a series of four around two-minute clips, and you just watch them all in a row.
它由四段两分钟左右的短片组成，你可以一口气看完。

636
00:26:31.890 --> 00:26:36.010
Clip one reveals Creed has decided to blackmail his co-workers.
第一段短片揭示了克里德决定勒索他的同事们。

637
00:26:36.030 --> 00:26:38.990
The first person he's going to try to blackmail is Oscar.
他第一个打算勒索的人是奥斯卡。

638
00:26:39.330 --> 00:26:47.090
So the opening scene is Oscar watching a video on a laptop of Creed, and then Creed walks in
